From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Domenico D'Arrigo <DCHEM88@hotmail.it>
Date: Sun, 25 Oct 2026 15:12:07 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mb/lenovo/haswell: Put CFG Lock and the processor objects in
 the setup

The C-state configuration lock goes to Energy Saver > Processor, after
the C-states; the form of the ACPI processor objects to General >
Advanced, next to the NMI option: both matter to the OS rather than to
the hardware. Their defaults keep what the firmware did so far.

TEST=Built lenovo/w541 with mrc.bin and with the native RAM init.

Co-authored-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_018n3yuWwDLW63F4vdf7ZFTv
---
 src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c | 2 ++
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
index e81dcf7130..2e8fc3e085 100644
--- a/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
+++ b/src/mainboard/lenovo/haswell/cfr.c
@@ -255,6 +255,7 @@ static const struct sm_object general_advanced = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 	.ui_name	= "Advanced",
 	.obj_list	= (const struct sm_object *[]) {
 		&nmi,
+		&acpi_cpu_objects,
 		NULL
 	},
 });
@@ -335,6 +336,7 @@ static const struct sm_object energy_processor = SM_DECLARE_FORM({
 		&eist,
 		&turbo_mode,
 		&c_states,
+		&cfg_lock,
 		&tdp_pl1_override,
 		&tdp_pl2_override,
 		&cpu_power_limit_lock,
-- 
2.43.0

